# Guard rail for the blog publishing automation.
#
# Any pull request that touches a path listed here needs approval from the
# owner before it can merge. Paths NOT listed — blog posts, the blog index,
# the sitemap — merge freely, which is exactly what the automation needs.
#
# This file is what stops an automated blog post from quietly editing the
# homepage, the stylesheet, or this guard itself. It is enforced by GitHub,
# not by instructions, so a misread playbook cannot get around it.
#
# Requires on the repo:
#   Settings > Branches > add a rule for `main`
#     [x] Require a pull request before merging
#         Required approvals: 0
#         [x] Require review from Code Owners
#     [x] Do not allow bypassing the above settings
#
# Without "Require a pull request before merging", anything can be pushed
# straight to main and none of this applies.

# --- Site chrome: changing these changes every page ---------------------
/index.html            @amit-retainia
/404.html              @amit-retainia
/assets/               @amit-retainia

# --- Hosting and crawler behaviour --------------------------------------
/_headers              @amit-retainia
/_redirects            @amit-retainia
/robots.txt            @amit-retainia
/netlify.toml          @amit-retainia

# --- The automation's own machinery -------------------------------------
# Left unguarded, a post could rewrite the rules it is judged by.
/.github/              @amit-retainia
/BLOG-PLAYBOOK.md      @amit-retainia
/blog/_TEMPLATE.html   @amit-retainia
/scripts/              @amit-retainia
/package.json          @amit-retainia
/package-lock.json     @amit-retainia

# --- Deliberately NOT listed, so publishing needs no approval -----------
#   /blog/<slug>/index.html   new posts
#   /blog/index.html          the card grid
#   /blog/images/             hero images
#   /sitemap.xml              url list
